# Input for the CI supply-chain integrity lock. Mirrors [project].dependencies
# from pyproject.toml. Compiled to requirements-lock.txt with pinned sha256
# hashes via: uv pip compile requirements.in --generate-hashes \
#   --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
#   -o requirements-lock.txt
# NOTE: this lock is for CI/dev reproducibility ONLY. Library installs resolve
# from pyproject.toml's abstract constraints -- do NOT pin hashes there.
#
# pandas, numpy, scipy, scikit-learn and statsmodels were dropped on
# 2026-09-08: nothing in src/ or tests/ imports them any more (the native
# arms replaced them), so the lock was hash-pinning a scientific stack the
# library never loads. The cross-validation stack now lives in
# requirements-parity.in, which is deliberately NOT hash-pinned in CI --
# it is a comparison harness, not a dependency.
